<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Garama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Garama, modern Germa in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a>. It was a planned town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> supported by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foggara">foggara</a> irrigation and trans-Saharan trade. By around 500 CE it had greatly declined.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/garama.jpg" alt="Garama" width="320" height="288" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franzfoto · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garma_(Garama)_-_Ruinen_der_antiken_Stadt_Garma_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>This agricultural surplus sustained a population estimated at around 10,000 in and around the capital <b>Garama</b> at its peak, an exceptional concentration for the central Sahara.</blockquote><a href="/empire/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
